{
  "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8044-9f34-ec7dca26258e",
  "title": "Relational Database Connections",
  "sourceUrl": "https://xpandeyed.notion.site/20924eb1ed5480449f34ec7dca26258e",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "relational-databases-lesson-0",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "JPA, Hibernate and Spring Data"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "relational-databases-lesson-0-note-0",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Jakarta Persistence, usually called JPA, defines how Java classes map to relational tables."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "relational-databases-lesson-0-note-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "An entity is one of these mapped classes."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "relational-databases-lesson-0-note-1-part-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "One entity object represents one stored row."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "relational-databases-lesson-0-note-2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Hibernate implements JPA."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "relational-databases-lesson-0-note-2-part-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "It reads the mappings and runs the SQL needed to load or change rows."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "relational-databases-lesson-0-note-3",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Spring Data JPA creates repository beans."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "relational-databases-lesson-0-note-3-part-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "A repository gives application code methods for saving and finding entities."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "relational-databases-lesson-0-note-4",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Spring Boot configures these libraries from the dependencies and database settings."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "relational-databases-lesson-0-note-5",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "The flow is service \u2192 repository \u2192 Hibernate \u2192 database."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "relational-databases-lesson-0-note-5-part-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Entity mapping comes next."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "relational-databases-lesson-0-note-5-part-2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Repository methods follow after that."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8088-bf3b-e2a5e1e9166f",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Database connections"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8088-bf3b-e2a5e1e9166f-note-0",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "A "
        ],
        [
          "DataSource",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " supplies the JDBC connections Hibernate uses."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8088-bf3b-e2a5e1e9166f-note-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Boot configures a "
        ],
        [
          "DataSource",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " when the application has a database driver and connection settings."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8088-bf3b-e2a5e1e9166f-note-2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "The JPA starter includes HikariCP."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8088-bf3b-e2a5e1e9166f-note-2-part-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Its connection pool reuses connections across operations."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8088-bf3b-e2a5e1e9166f-note-3",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "The JDBC URL selects the database."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8088-bf3b-e2a5e1e9166f-note-3-part-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Boot usually identifies the driver from that URL."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8088-bf3b-e2a5e1e9166f-note-4",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Boot connects to a PostgreSQL server."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8088-bf3b-e2a5e1e9166f-note-4-part-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "It does not install or start that server."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8088-bf3b-e2a5e1e9166f-example-0",
      "type": "example",
      "example": {
        "title": "Configure the employee database",
        "language": "text",
        "description": [
          "The tabs contain all application files for this separate Maven project.",
          "The example requires Java 17 or later, Maven and PostgreSQL with an existing `employee_notes` database.",
          "The environment supplies `DB_USERNAME` and `DB_PASSWORD`.",
          "`database/schema.sql` creates the tables in an empty database before `mvn spring-boot:run`.",
          "Hibernate validates the supplied schema. It does not create the tables."
        ],
        "code": "",
        "explanation": [
          "Boot manages the dependency versions through its parent or dependency management.",
          "`spring.datasource.*` supplies the connection settings.",
          "`validate` checks that mapped tables and columns exist.",
          "It does not create them.",
          "`spring.jpa.open-in-view=false` keeps later entity loading out of web response rendering.",
          "Relationship loading is explained after relationships."
        ],
        "files": [
          {
            "name": "src/main/resources/application.properties",
            "language": "text",
            "code": "spring.datasource.url=jdbc:postgresql://localhost:5432/employee_notes\nspring.datasource.username=${DB_USERNAME}\nspring.datasource.password=${DB_PASSWORD}\nspring.jpa.hibernate.ddl-auto=validate\nspring.jpa.open-in-view=false\n"
          },
          {
            "name": "src/main/java/com/example/demo/employee/Employee.java",
            "language": "java",
            "code": "package com.example.demo.employee;\n\nimport jakarta.persistence.Column;\nimport jakarta.persistence.Entity;\nimport jakarta.persistence.GeneratedValue;\nimport jakarta.persistence.GenerationType;\nimport jakarta.persistence.Id;\nimport jakarta.persistence.Table;\n\n@Entity\n@Table(name = \"employees\")\npublic class Employee {\n    @Id\n    @GeneratedValue(strategy = GenerationType.IDENTITY)\n    private Long id;\n\n    @Column(nullable = false, length = 100)\n    private String name;\n\n    @Column(nullable = false, length = 100)\n    private String department;\n\n    protected Employee() {}\n\n    public Employee(String name, String department) {\n        this.name = name;\n        this.department = department;\n    }\n\n    public Long getId() { return id; }\n    public String getName() { return name; }\n    public String getDepartment() { return department; }\n    public void rename(String name) { this.name = name; }\n}\n"
          },
          {
            "name": "pom.xml",
            "language": "text",
            "code": "<project xmlns=\"http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0\" xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\"\n         xsi:schemaLocation=\"http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd\">\n    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>\n    <parent>\n        <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n        <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-parent</artifactId>\n        <version>3.5.16</version>\n        <relativePath/>\n    </parent>\n    <groupId>com.example</groupId>\n    <artifactId>demo</artifactId>\n    <version>1.0.0</version>\n    <properties><java.version>17</java.version></properties>\n    <dependencies>\n        <dependency>\n            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-data-jpa</artifactId>\n        </dependency>\n        <dependency>\n            <groupId>org.postgresql</groupId>\n            <artifactId>postgresql</artifactId>\n            <scope>runtime</scope>\n        </dependency>\n    </dependencies>\n    <build>\n        <finalName>demo</finalName>\n        <plugins>\n            <plugin>\n                <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n                <artifactId>spring-boot-maven-plugin</artifactId>\n            </plugin>\n        </plugins>\n    </build>\n\n</project>\n"
          },
          {
            "name": "src/main/java/com/example/demo/DemoApplication.java",
            "language": "java",
            "code": "package com.example.demo;\n\nimport org.springframework.boot.SpringApplication;\nimport org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.SpringBootApplication;\n\n@SpringBootApplication\npublic class DemoApplication {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        SpringApplication.run(DemoApplication.class, args);\n    }\n}\n"
          },
          {
            "name": "database/schema.sql",
            "language": "sql",
            "code": "CREATE TABLE employees (\n    id BIGINT GENERATED BY DEFAULT AS IDENTITY PRIMARY KEY,\n    name VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,\n    department VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL\n);\n"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "relational-databases-lesson-2",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Schema changes"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "relational-databases-lesson-2-note-0",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "spring.jpa.hibernate.ddl-auto",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " controls Hibernate schema handling."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "relational-databases-lesson-2-note-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "none",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " leaves the schema unchanged."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "relational-databases-lesson-2-note-1-part-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "validate",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " checks it against the entity mappings."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "relational-databases-lesson-2-note-2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "create",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " recreates the mapped schema."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "relational-databases-lesson-2-note-2-part-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "create-drop",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " also drops it at normal shutdown."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "relational-databases-lesson-2-note-2-part-2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Both can destroy existing data."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "relational-databases-lesson-2-note-3",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Flyway and Liquibase apply ordered migration files to a persistent database."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "relational-databases-lesson-2-note-4",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "update",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " changes a schema automatically."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "relational-databases-lesson-2-note-4-part-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "It does not provide the reviewable change history of migrations."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "relational-databases-lesson-3",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "H2 as a separate local database"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "relational-databases-lesson-3-note-0",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Boot can configure an embedded H2 database when the runtime dependency "
        ],
        [
          "com.h2database:h2",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " is present."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "relational-databases-lesson-3-note-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "An in-memory H2 database loses its data when it closes."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "relational-databases-lesson-3-note-2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "H2 replaces PostgreSQL for that local case."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "relational-databases-lesson-3-note-2-part-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Its behavior does not establish that PostgreSQL-specific SQL works."
        ]
      ]
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Understand the data libraries, then configure the relational connection used by the employee examples.",
  "updatedOn": "2026-10-20",
